#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087722 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087523 :question/id #uuid "a792fa16-e1fd-5f30-a128-bbc49a285429" :question/math-academy-id "e-5099" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=t^2-6t, \\,\\,\\, y=t^4+4, \\quad t \\in (-\\infty , \\infty),\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ we can start by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={t}^{2}-6t \\\\  & ={(t-3)}^{2}-(3)^{2} \\\\  & ={(t-3)}^{2}-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\left( t-3\\right)^2 \\geq 0,$ we can conclude that $x \\geq -9.$\n\n- To find the range of $y=t^4+4,$ notice that $t^4 \\geq 0,$ and consequently $y \\geq 4.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $x \\geq -9$ and $y \\geq 4.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cbf0ad0-a7c5-5c0f-a06c-9210fdc244ef" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050372 :topic/math-academy-id 450 :topic/title "Completing the Square"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050580 :topic/math-academy-id 3728 :topic/title "The Range of a Function: Advanced Cases"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050642 :topic/math-academy-id 1875 :topic/title "Properties of Transformed Square Root Functions"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088030 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b66d32e-948b-514c-b79f-7024a2f95a75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\ge 0, y \\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084915} {:answer/id #uuid "da35ba7d-f113-5b40-a7a6-b2c42bd62346" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\le 9, y \\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084916} {:answer/id #uuid "258a9d84-41a0-5795-96ec-43227eb669e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\ge - 9, y \\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084917} {:answer/id #uuid "5ebf0762-ff4f-5c76-b927-68997ac64c9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :a