\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ generate a circle of radius $1$ centered at the point $(3,2)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +a,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +b,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have a circle of radius $1$ centered at the point $(3,2).$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088355 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86fe87b2-1a29-514a-a9ac-dc3d112601b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 8\\cos θ + 2, y = 8\\sin θ - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086784} {:answer/id #uuid "c398c05e-f448-56ee-b77e-39a233b8ec93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 2\\cos θ - 1, y = 2\\sin θ + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086785} {:answer/id #uuid "f494b146-ee7b-5a88-8454-86ca6ef09d22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 2\\sin θ - 1, y = 2\\cos θ + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086786} {:answer/id #uuid "fc5ac71e-b176-5974-b918-42f96e049f19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 4\\cos θ - 1, y = 4\\sin θ + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086787} {:answer/id #uuid "1da49f45-a0a9-5fc2-bddf-eea16266efa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 4\\sin θ - 1, y = 4\\cos θ + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086788}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5ce892d5-8689-5495-aab0-0fd1245afd68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086783}] :question/id #uuid "2e73cbbe-2cd3-5191-8a77-e313eca872b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-78205" :question/problem "![](images/d6/d63963154e858da324418ef8f29aa8e4f309355b7cd6ad105a89f96506027248.png)\n\nConsider the circle of radius $2$ centered at $(-1, 2)$, as shown abo